WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:05.370
If I make the judge eat it
before the crispiness disappears,

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.380
I’m sure to win.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.540
All right!

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.550
I’m done!

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.050
Whether it’s a tart or a croissant,

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.800
the pie-type, crispy crust is best when it’s just baked,

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.040
and definitely more delicious if eaten immediately.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.500
But... both have finished
making the tart at the same time!

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.520
In that case, eat both together!

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:57.750
C... Could it be that I asked for
something that I shouldn’t have?

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.100
Th-This is bad, guys!

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.510
Wh-What is it this time?

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:04.850
To make him eat two breads at the same time...

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.230
Something terrible is going to happen.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.240
We are all going to be pulled into this reaction.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.800
Wh-What was that?

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.790
Wh-What’s...

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:29.540
What’s going to happen to us?!

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.420
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.380
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.590
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:48.270
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.520
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:02.560
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:08.730
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:23.870
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:32.420
probably helped me notice that

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:38.340
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:47.190
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:52.610
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:59.700
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:05.540
that white sky with my colors.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:12.540
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.880
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.960
This is the path I must take!?

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.750
The Road of the Loquat!

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:44.190
Wh... Where...

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.810
am I?

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:51.190
Kawachi!

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.740
Are you all right, Kawachi?!

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.360
Kawachi!

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.290
You’re heavy, you dork!

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:01.300
But... Where the hell is this?

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.920
We’ve walked quite a bit, but
we haven’t run into anybody.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.310
What are you doing?!

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.300
I’m hungry...

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:14.220
I was looking to see if there was any food lying around.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.990
Don’t eat stuff that’s lying
on the ground!

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:20.720
It’s a loquat!

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.560
There’s a loquat preserved in
brown sugar lying over here!

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.390
Huh?

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.150
Why is something like that lying there?

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.190
Isn’t it rotten or something?

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:26.980
It’s all right.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:27.600
We can eat it.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:35.170
I’m going to control you.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.090
Did you say something?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:38.960
Nope.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.180
What’s wrong?

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.680
No, it’s just...

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.180
The loquat’s become a ring and I can’t get it off.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.060
What was that?!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.560
Heave-ho!

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.480
I can’t make <i>Japan</i> like this.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:08.870
Hey!

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.160
Help us!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.660
Hey, over here!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:14.870
What’s wrong?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.170
Something doesn’t feel right.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:27.930
Kawachi!

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:30.800
What are you doing?!

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:31.970
Run away quickly!

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.570
Come on, stand up.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.240
Are you hurt?

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.740
Aren’t you Tsukino?!

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.120
You’re right!

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.750
Why is Tsukino here?

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:58.750
My name is Moon.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.580
I am the Elf Princess.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.000
You’re Dorif’s beard?

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:04.510
That loquat!

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:07.010
It’s stuck to my finger
and I can’t get it off.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.300
I was right then.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.060
If we stay here,
we might be attacked again.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.010
We should first return to our castle,

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:17.180
and there, you should meet the the great sage Meistrof.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.440
I see.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.280
Doesn’t he look exactly like Old Man Meister?

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:27.660
Isn’t he Meister, in fact?

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.400
That is definitely

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:33.660
the magical loquat created by
Snowzer in order to take over the world.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.280
Snowzer?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.790
A magical loquat?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:37.670
That’s right.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:41.080
It is a loquat that was
betrayed by the Snow Queen, Snowzer.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:45.210
The loquat now has a will of its own
and wishes to get revenge on her

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.720
by using human greed to
defeat her and then rule the world.

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:53.390
Our peace is on the verge of destruction.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.850
In order to save this world,

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:59.690
we need to defeat Queen Snowzer
and then destroy that loquat.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.980
Is that so?

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.940
Well, leaving aside the matter of
the necessity to defeat Snowzer...

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.190
Why do we also need
to destroy this loquat?

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.740
That is because, even should
we manage to defeat Snowzer,

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:13.450
we cannot allow that loquat’s
evil powers to remain in this world.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.330
Right now, the people of this world
are suffering under Snowzer’s power.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.960
We have to do something as soon as possible.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.670
That’s terrible.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.460
Yeah.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.170
But, it sounds really complicated.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.590
All right.

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.210
In that case, I’ll do something.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.800
Really?

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:31.470
Yeah.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.180
Uh... Azuma-kun?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.390
So, what should I do?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.180
He’s ignoring me.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:37.890
You must defeat Snowzer.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.100
And then, you must destroy the
magical loquat by throwing it into

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:44.900
her castle’s trash can on the “day for burnable trash,” which comes only once a year.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.650
Of course, this is impossible for
just the two of you to carry out.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:48.190
So...

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.740
The man who can crack even boulders with his fist,

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.660
Ken...

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:00.410
And the great archer, Crownie, who can split apart
boulders from 5 km away with his arrow of light...
Note: Kanmuri (<b>冠) means “crown.”</b>

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.570
And I, Meistrof,

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:09.920
who can annihilate even boulders with my lightning strike, Thunderstorm.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.180
This handy threesome shall
accompany you.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.890
They really resemble them.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:18.180
But...

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.140
Why do they all specialize in boulders?

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:23.640
Kazuma, step forward.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:24.900
What is it?

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.690
This is the Holy Powder of Light.

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.820
I’m sure that if will come to your aid when needed.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.280
It has the same smell as flour
with super-high protein content!

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:39.950
Huh?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.160
Come!

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:45.720
The annual “day for burnable trash”
comes in three days!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.420
But...

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.130
It really doesn’t feel like we’re walking with strangers.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:52.920
Yeah...

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.590
What’s the matter, Kanmuri?

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.140
I mean... Crownie...

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.490
Oh?!
What’s that?!

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:06.190
They are Snowzer’s minions.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.690
They fear the revenge of the
loquat and seek to destroy it.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.150
They are aiming for Kazuma’s loquat!

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:15.150
We must protect Kazuma!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.910
I’m pushed to the side?!

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.550
They’re really strong!

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.640
It’s the old man from the loquat market!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:44.850
You’re right!

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.440
He is Golem.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.350
He is the owner of the magical loquat.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:50.070
This belongs to him?

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.400
My precious!

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.030
Ever since his loquat
was stolen by Snowzer,

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.660
he has been wandering in search of it

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.500
and has been suffering under her,
like the people of this land.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.040
You poor thing.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.470
Yeah, Snowzer sounds heinous.

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:13.750
My precious...

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.090
Say, you want to come with us?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.180
Is that all right?

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.850
Well, didn’t the loquat originally belong to him?

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:24.220
In that case, I’d like for him to be with it a little longer.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:25.810
Right?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.690
Master, I’ll come with you.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:31.690
I know a shortcut to Snowzer’s castle.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:33.440
You will guide us?

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.940
Yes, yes, yes.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.560
It’s so cold here, I’m about to freeze.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.060
That’s a sign we’re close
to Snowzer’s castle.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:09.270
The closer we get to Snowzer’s castle,

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.480
the stronger the loquat’s power will get.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.690
Especially during the time that we sleep.

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.070
Be careful that you do not get possessed.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.320
What do you mean?

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:18.570
It is said that...

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:24.280
the loquat attempts to gain control over its
owner by luring him in with enticing dreams.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:25.910
So while it may be a dream,

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.540
be careful not to give in to the
sweet temptation of the loquat.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:29.870
Is that so?!

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.540
In that case, I won’t sleep anymore!

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.010
Hey, you!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:39.670
Kid!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:40.550
Hey, kid!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:42.050
Here, here.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.140
Not there.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:45.600
Here!

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:48.520
Hello there!

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:50.640
The loquat is talking!

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.310
What is it that you wish for?

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.610
Money? Women? Power?

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.520
I can grant anything you wish for.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:58.780
Oh?

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.490
You’re amazing, huh?

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:01.530
Right?

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:05.030
My wish, I guess, is...

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.830
No matter who it is, human
beings always desire something.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:12.240
Come now.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.660
Tell me what your dirty little desire is.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.080
I will control your heart.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.540
It’s to make the <i>Japan</i>!

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.880
<i>J... Japan</i>?

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.050
What is that?

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.170
You see...

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:28.050
France has French bread and
England has English bread, right?

00:12:28.650 --> 00:12:29.800
So, I...

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:31.810
I want to make <i>Japan</i> in my country.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.640
Oh!

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:34.680
I see...

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:35.930
It’s a weird wish,

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:37.980
but there’s nothing that I can’t do.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.020
I will make that bread for you.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:41.320
No, that’s fine.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.530
I mean...

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:47.570
If I don’t make it by working hard
on my own, it’s not fun or anything.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.990
Hmm... Th-That might be true.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:51.330
Then...

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.740
Just tell me what your other desires are.

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:56.000
Don’t have any.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.410
Don’t have any?!

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.670
That’s ridiculous.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.540
Everyone has multiple desires!

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.670
Not much use in telling me that...

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:08.180
Then, do you have any, old man?

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.340
Desires, I mean.

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:10.220
Me?

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.050
Of course!

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:15.220
I want to defeat Snowzer
and gain control over this world.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.640
What will you do after you gain control?

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.270
After I gain control...?

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:27.860
I dunno.

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:29.240
Don’t you wish for anything else?

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.910
Uh... Anything else?

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.650
Well...

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.500
You won’t laugh?

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:39.290
I won’t laugh. So tell me.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.210
Well, in the end I am a loquat.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.470
So, I guess... I want people
to eat me like I am delicious...

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:49.680
All right, I’ll eat you then.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.270
Hey, wait wait wait!

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:52.890
Don’t make fun of me!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:55.060
While I may be a loquat, I’m a <i>magical</i> loquat!

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.270
I can’t bear to be eaten like a regular one.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:01.100
Loquats have it hard too, huh?

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:02.440
Yeah, we have issues of our own.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:05.230
Okay then! Next time, I’ll use you in my Tart <i>Japan</i>!

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:06.730
Huh? Tart <i>Japan</i>?

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:07.900
Yep!

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.280
It’s made with black loquats just like you, old man.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.030
With black loquats?

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.570
Does it taste good?

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:16.240
Yeah, it’s delicious!
It’s <i>Japan</i>, after all...

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:17.790
I see...

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:23.500
Well, with these warm hands you
should be able to make something delicious.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:27.000
Yep! That’s ’cause I have the Solar Hands!

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.260
The Solar Hands?!

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:29.630
In that case...

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:33.770
Someday, would you use those
hands to make a Tart <i>Japan</i> with me?

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:35.770
Yep! It’s a promise!

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.520
Until then, I won’t leave you.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:41.230
Is that so?

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:43.350
Azuma!

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.360
Azuma!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.400
Azuma! Azuma!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.530
Wake up, Kazuma!

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.490
You’ve come to?

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:54.280
Huh?

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:55.700
The loquat?

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:57.910
You... Your hand...

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:03.170
You were almost controlled by it.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.000
Controlled?

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.420
I don’t think he would do that.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.960
If he were to, I wouldn’t be able to keep my promise.

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.340
Promise?

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.630
Either way, this loquat seems like a pretty nice guy.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.970
What are you talking about?

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.260
If we hadn’t woken you up, your whole body would’ve been swallowed up by it.

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:20.560
You must not underestimate a magical loquat!

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:31.940
We’re here.

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:34.530
This is Snowzer’s castle.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:37.200
Today is the annual
“day for burnable trash.”

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:48.880
Kazuma!

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:57.590
Leave this to me!

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:58.390
Go!

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:13.570
What?!

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:16.320
Crownie!

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:22.330
Impressive that you’ve come
this far, you little cockroaches.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:23.880
She’s here!

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.080
The Snow Queen, Snowzer!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.550
Now all we have to do is defeat her!

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.050
Thunderstorm!

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:41.310
Did he get her?!

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:47.480
How futile.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.190
Take this!

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.280
Blizzard Hands!

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:55.780
Old Man Meistrof!

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:00.450
Kawachi!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.250
You can disappear together with the loquat.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.260
Secret Technique!
Reverse Folding Technique!

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:14.760
I’m sure that it will come to your aid when needed.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:15.960
That’s right!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:22.930
Cheap little tricks!

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:24.140
Then how’s this?!

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:38.650
Loquat Final Dimension!

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:41.780
The Jet Black Weapon!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.580
Take this!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:50.710
Still more to come!

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:55.300
It’s no use!

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.630
Don’t give up!

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:59.090
You’re not allowed to die until you fulfill your promise!

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:01.890
What is this?

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:02.760
Now!

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.470
Hold up those Solar Hands!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:05.810
O-Okay.

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.480
What is this light?!

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:22.030
Why?

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:24.700
How could a mere loquat...?!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.580
It’s not me!

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:29.710
This boy’s love is going to thwart your dark aspirations!

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.460
Love?!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.960
This boy has conviction and love toward all ingredients.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:40.050
He can make even a loquat like me taste delicious!

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:41.380
And...

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:44.470
He taught me the joy of living as a loquat.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.180
There’s no way that someone like you,

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:49.180
without a shred of love
inside you, could win against him!

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:52.190
You cheeky little loquat!

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:17.710
No!

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.960
I promised him!

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:22.220
That I would make him
into a Tart <i>Japan</i>!

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:24.010
What are you talking about?!

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:27.680
If we don’t throw him into the
trash can, peace cannot return!

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:31.140
And... How long do I have to stay frozen?

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.180
No!

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.440
I’m definitely going to make
the loquat into my Tart <i>Japan</i>!

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:37.400
Kazuma...

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:41.440
I’m just happy that you feel that way.

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:42.400
Loquat!

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:46.240
If I’m to disappear, all magic will disappear as well.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:48.450
And you’ll be able to return
to your world.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.950
If you don’t return to your world,

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.530
you can’t make your dream... the <i>Japan</i>.

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.710
Come, destroy me...

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:00.460
Throw me into the trash can.

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:02.970
No! I said no!

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.930
Farewell, Kazuma.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.970
Loquat! Don’t!

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:13.980
It was short, but it was fun.

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:15.980
We must part here.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:17.770
But, I...

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:20.190
will never forget the warmth of your Solar Hands,

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:23.990
your kindness... and your love.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.030
You must live on, pursuing the dream of your <i>Japan</i>.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.990
That is the road you must follow.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:36.250
And someday... when I’m reborn as a loquat...

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:39.290
Make your Tart <i>Japan</i> with me.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:41.630
It’s a promise.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:45.510
That’s the road a loquat must take.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:47.010
In other words...

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:50.430
The Road of the Loquat!

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:56.350
Loquat.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:20:59.520
Loquat!

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:00.940
Oh? This wasn’t the Lord of the Rings?
Loquat!

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.900
Oh? This wasn’t the Lord of the Rings?

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:04.900
It was the Road of the Loquat?!

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:08.280
Winner: Pantasia!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.240
So, all that was a reaction?!

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.290
All right.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.370
He did it!

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:16.040
Yay.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.750
Good work!

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.510
Thank you kid!

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:27.010
T-To think that I’d lose...

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:34.060
It’s true that St. Pierre’s strawberry tart,
made with the Reverse Folding Technique,

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:38.020
superbly matched the strawberries with the crust,
and was wonderful in terms of technical skill!

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:39.400
But!

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.820
With croissant dough made crispy by
using super-high protein content flour,

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:46.240
as well as loquats preserved in
brown sugar, it is no exaggeration...

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.990
to call Pantasia’s tart a miraculous taste!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:50.320
And...

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:52.240
What made it possible is...

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:55.740
Azuma Kazuma’s Solar Hands!

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.410
These hands can be called

00:21:57.410 --> 00:22:01.000
hands that can represent his
love toward food and its ingredients!

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:04.710
Is that so?

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:06.510
But, Kuro-yan...

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:09.270
No matter what, wasn’t the reaction a little too long?

00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:11.220
That is my road...

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:13.970
The Road of the Kuroyanagi!

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:16.010
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:18.980
And, why am I still slightly frozen?

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:21.900
That is the Road of the Kawachi!

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:23.980
Why the hell is my road so steep?!

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:30.240
Well, all’s well that ends well.

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:31.820
It hasn’t ended well at all!

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:33.030
Azuma! Azuma!

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:34.740
You listening to me?! Hey!

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:44.090
Robbie, come on out to the sound of the voice calling you.

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:52.010
Robbie, you were crying all by yourself.

00:22:52.180 --> 00:23:00.350
Robbie, the eyes in your heart...

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:03.820
what is it that they reflect?

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:07.240
...Is it “Who am I?”...

00:23:07.610 --> 00:23:15.030
The other side of the mirage flickers faintly.

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:23.630
Anywhere is fine, as long as it’s not here.

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:32.340
My dancing heart is reborn as a marble time and again.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:36.470
The colors I just filled in were yours.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:40.390
It’s not something that will finish with a turn. Be load.

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:48.320
Just like your joy, try letting your tears flow.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:52.410
See? The world is filled in with your colors.

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:59.080
Like a tumble, do the best of you.

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:08.010
It... It... It’s the last episode, you say?!

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:09.470
It’s the last episode, huh?

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:10.880
Yep, it’s the last episode.

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:12.350
Yeah, it’s the last episode.

00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:13.600
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan:

00:24:13.600 --> 00:24:14.810
The last episode!

00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:16.940
Who is it that you will give truly delicious bread to!?

00:24:16.940 --> 00:24:18.430
The <i>Japan</i>, forever!

00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:19.970
Be absolutely sure to watch.

